  "raw": {
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3A2948EF284B8722FEE42E01FB156C27/jobs/81146": {
      "title": "Physician Assistant Medical Director, Boston Campus",
      "description": "Physician Assistant Medical Director, Boston Campus You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Physician Assistant Medical Director, Boston Campus Hot Job Boston, MA 02129 Start Date   06/04/2026 Apply Overview Salary Range $60,000.00 - $60,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Part-Time Faculty Apply Description Status: Part-time, 12 months Location: Boston campus Key Responsibilities: Support the Program Director by providing review and critique of curriculum, courses, and clinical rotations to ensure the didactic and clinical phases of the PA Program meet current and acceptable practice standards. Hold an active interest in the PA program and help guide it through future endeavors by actively participating in program affairs, allotting time for regular meetings with the Program Director, faculty, and students Serve as an advocate for both the PA Program and the PA profession. Recruit instructors as requested by the academic coordinator and clinical sites as requested by the clinical coordinator. Participate in the admissions process and applicant selection. Help develop and/or revise and maintain program mission statements, competencies, goals, and policies in accordance with ARC-PA Standards of Accreditation. Support the development and review of the program curriculum and competencies to meet current practice standards as they relate to the PA role. Qualifications Qualifications: Hold, at minimum, an earned Doctorate degree in Allopathic or Osteopathic Medicine or be a currently or previously licensed Physician Assistant. Be currently or previously licensed as an Allopathic or Osteopathic Physician by the State Board of Medical Examiners or as a Physician Assistant. Hold current or previous Board Certification by an ABMS or AOA approved specialty board as an Allopathic or Osteopathic physician. (It is desirable that the candidate be board certified in Family Medicine, Internal Medicine, or an Internal Medicine subspecialty). Minimum 3 years of practice experience. Be knowledgeable in current practice standards and the physician assistant role. Compensation : $60,000/annually All correspondence relating to the position of Physician Assistant Medical Director, Boston Campus at Bay Path University should be directed in confidence to the University’s executive search consultant: Adam Barrett, Associate Vice President Scott Healy & Associates adam@scotthealy.com A complete application should include the following: 1.    Cover Letter outlining your interest and qualifications for the position; 2.    Updated CV; 3.    Contact information for three (3) professional references with title, institutional affiliation, email address and direct phone numbers. (No references will be contacted without written permission from the candidate.) Applications received by July 17, 2026 will receive priority consideration. The search will remain open until the position is filled. Share job details to About BAY PATH UNIVERSITY Bay Path University is a private comprehensive university with a bold and innovative spirit. Known for its commitment to providing a practical and career-focused education, Bay Path offers a residential bachelors degree for women only on its Longmeadow, Massachusetts campus, as well as bachelors, masters and doctoral programs for both men and women on campuses in East Longmeadow, Boston, Guaynabo, Puerto Rico and online. In 2024, Bay Path expanded its reach and program offerings through the acquisition of Cambridge College, increasing its enrollment to approximately 5,000 learners, gaining new locations, strengthening its online presence, and broadening its career-focused programs. Respected for strong allied health, education and business programs, accessible online options, and a supportive community, Bay Path is an appealing choice for many students. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3A2948EF284B8722FEE42E01FB156C27/jobs/119110": {
      "title": "Coordinator & Assistant to the Dean, School of Health & Natural Science",
      "description": "Coordinator & Assistant to the Dean, School of Health & Natural Science You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Coordinator & Assistant to the Dean, School of Health & Natural Science East Longmeadow, MA 01028 Apply Overview Salary Range $23.00 - $27.68 Hourly Position Type Full-Time Hourly Apply Description Position Summary The Administrative Assistant and Coordinator to the Dean provides administrative, operational, and project coordination support to the Dean of the School of Health and Natural Sciences (SHNS). The Coordinator serves as a key point of contact for faculty, staff, students, University offices, and external partners, and supports the effective day-to-day operations of the Dean’s Office and the Philip H. Ryan Health Center. This is a full-time, on-site position with regular hours of Monday through Friday, 8:30 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. The position requires an on-campus presence, with occasional evening and weekend hours as needed to support School and University activities. The position requires strong organizational, communication, and problem-solving skills; the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines; and discretion in handling confidential information. Under the direction of the Dean, the Coordinator also supports School-wide projects and strategic initiatives by coordinating activities, maintaining timelines, tracking deliverables, and facilitating follow-up. Essential Job Functions : Provides superior customer service within all levels of the organization, SHNS, and the Philip H Ryan Health Center. Support the Dean as the project manager in SHNS as needed. Maintain and track the School’s work plan, including key initiatives, responsibilities, deadlines, and deliverables, and provide regular updates to the Dean. Responsible for researching information needed for School and University reports, analyzing and synthesizing information gathered. Must be able to work collaboratively across sites with other staff on a daily basis. Handles confidential information and uses the highest discretion regarding sensitive matters. Administrative and Operational Support Manage the Dean’s calendar, meetings, appointments, interviews, and School-related activities (i.e., department budgets, contracts, position postings, PCO process, and Workload forms). Coordinate SHNS and departmental meetings, including scheduling, agendas, materials, meeting notes, and follow-up. Prepare correspondence, reports, presentations, summaries, and other materials for the Dean. Collaborate with the  Assistant Dean and school program leaders as necessary or as directed by the SHNS Dean Respond to and appropriately direct inquiries from students, faculty, staff, prospective students, University offices, and external partners. Assist with School events, recruitment activities, faculty and staff searches, onboarding, and new-hire documentation. Maintain accurate School and Dean’s Office records, files, calendars, and communication platforms. Coordinate operational needs, supplies, equipment, facilities, and related activities for the Dean’s Office and Ryan Health Science Center, as assigned. Coordinate and oversee the day-to-day management of supplies, equipment, and facilities for the Ryan Health Science Center, as appropriate, to include maintenance, inventory management, logistics, security, and related activities. Work with Business Assistants and student work study positions covering the Ryan Center's operations. Handle confidential and sensitive information with discretion and professionalism. Project Management and School Initiatives Support the Dean in planning and coordinating School-wide projects, Ryan Center events, strategic priorities, program development, partnerships, recruitment initiatives, and special projects. Develop and maintain project plans, timelines, work plans, and action-item trackers. Track deadlines, milestones, deliverables, responsibilities, and outstanding items and provide timely follow-up. Maintain a master School calendar of projects, reports, accreditation activities, events, and key University deadlines. Coordinate project meetings and document decisions, responsibilities, next steps, and completion dates. Monitor project progress and bring upcoming deadlines, delays, risks, or items requiring decisions to the Dean’s attention. Support implementation and tracking of the SHNS strategic plan and preparation of progress reports and annual updates. Coordinate activities across academic programs, University departments, campuses, and external partners. Data, Program, and Communication Support Research, collect, analyze, and summarize information for School and University reports, projects, and decision-making. Assist with enrollment reporting, data verification, benchmarking, environmental scans, and competitive program research. Maintain and distribute current program information, academic grids, reports, and School-wide communications. Support recruitment and enrollment initiatives through data tracking, coordination, and communication with academic programs and University offices. Prepare materials and coordinate logistics for faculty and staff interviews and other School activities. Collaborate with SHNS program administrative assistants and coordinators to support consistent communication and efficient School operations. Perform other related duties and special projects as assigned by the Dean or the University. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in a related field or equivalent education and experience. Minimum of three (3) years’ experience as an office manager, administrative assistant, or higher-level support position. Experience with project management and ability to use project management tools. Ability to handle confidential information with integrity and discretion, and within FERPA and HIPAA guidelines. Experience working with department budgets, purchasing process, vendors, and contracts. High level of initiative, organizational, and time management skills. Must be detail-oriented with demonstrated attention to detail. Able to handle frequent interruptions, able to multitask, and pivot with different priorities. Excellent written and communication skills. Strong Microsoft Office Suite and Google Suite skills as well as working knowledge of database systems, data retrieval, and reporting. Excellent written and oral communication skills; must be able to independently generate memos and reports; a sense of humor and a collegial attitude. Must be self-directed with critical thinking skills and the ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team. Ability to effectively prioritize multiple responsibilities and adhere to deadlines. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with all members of the University community including students, faculty, staff, and administrators Ability to adhere to University policies and procedures. Ability to handle confidential information with discretion and within FERPA and HIPAA guidelines. All new employees must complete the FERPA, Anti-Harassment, and any other required online trainings within 15 days of employment. General knowledge of the University’s mission, purpose and goals and the role this position plays in achieving those goals. Share job details to About BAY PATH UNIVERSITY Bay Path University is a private comprehensive university with a bold and innovative spirit. Known for its commitment to providing a practical and career-focused education, Bay Path offers a residential bachelors degree for women only on its Longmeadow, Massachusetts campus, as well as bachelors, masters and doctoral programs for both men and women on campuses in East Longmeadow, Boston, Guaynabo, Puerto Rico and online. In 2024, Bay Path expanded its reach and program offerings through the acquisition of Cambridge College, increasing its enrollment to approximately 5,000 learners, gaining new locations, strengthening its online presence, and broadening its career-focused programs. Respected for strong allied health, education and business programs, accessible online options, and a supportive community, Bay Path is an appealing choice for many students. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
