    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3A2948EF284B8722FEE42E01FB156C27/jobs/118123": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Science",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Science You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Faculty - Science Longmeadow, MA 01106 Apply Overview Salary Range $500.00 - $1,200.00 Commission Position Type Adjunct Faculty Job Shift Day Apply Description Bay Path University seeks a qualified Adjunct Instructor to teach Anatomy and Physiology I (3 credits) in a face-to-face format. This course provides an overview of tissue types and their identification and function, as well as the integument, skeletal and muscular human body systems.The successful candidate will provide high-quality instruction to undergraduate students, fostering a supportive and engaging learning environment that promotes student success in foundational physics concepts. It is one section on Mondays and Wednesdays 9:30am to 10:45am Teach Anatomy and Physiology I lecture Develop and deliver lectures, demonstrations, and problem-solving sessions Prepare course materials, including syllabus, assignments, and assessments Evaluate and grade student work in a timely manner Maintain regular office hours and provide academic support to students Use the university’s learning management system to post materials and grades Collaborate with department faculty as needed Compensation: $500 - $1,200 per credit. Adjunct faculty pay rates vary, depending on academic discipline and the course's credit load and level. Qualifications Master’s degree in Biology or a closely related field (Ph.D. preferred) Prior teaching experience at the college level or strong evidence of teaching ability Strong communication and interpersonal skills Commitment to inclusive teaching practices and student engagement Ability to adhere to University policies and procedures Ability to handle confidential information with discretion and within FERPA and HIPAA guidelines. All new employees must complete the FERPA, Anti-Harassment, and any other required online trainings within 15 days of employment General knowledge of the University’s mission, purpose, and goals and the role this position plays in achieving those goals Share job details to About BAY PATH UNIVERSITY Bay Path University is a private comprehensive university with a bold and innovative spirit. Known for its commitment to providing a practical and career-focused education, Bay Path offers a residential bachelors degree for women only on its Longmeadow, Massachusetts campus, as well as bachelors, masters and doctoral programs for both men and women on campuses in East Longmeadow, Boston, Guaynabo, Puerto Rico and online. In 2024, Bay Path expanded its reach and program offerings through the acquisition of Cambridge College, increasing its enrollment to approximately 5,000 learners, gaining new locations, strengthening its online presence, and broadening its career-focused programs. Respected for strong allied health, education and business programs, accessible online options, and a supportive community, Bay Path is an appealing choice for many students. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
