    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3A2948EF284B8722FEE42E01FB156C27/jobs/116427": {
      "title": "Coordinator and Assistant to the Dean, Puerto Rico Campus",
      "description": "Coordinator and Assistant to the Dean, Puerto Rico Campus You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Coordinator and Assistant to the Dean, Puerto Rico Campus San Patricio Guaynabo Apply Overview Salary Range $23.00 - $25.00 Hourly Position Type Full-Time Hourly Apply Description Status: Full Time Hours : 37.5 hours per week, weekends required Job Location: Puerto Rico (on campus) Exempt (Yes/No): No JOB SUMMARY: The Coordinator & Assistant to the Dean provides experienced, high-level administrative and operational support to the Dean of the Puerto Rico Campus. This role requires the ability to work independently, exercise sound judgment, and manage competing priorities in a dynamic environment. The Coordinator serves as a key point of contact between the Dean's office and students, faculty, staff, government agencies, and University partners, and plays an active role in supporting the institutional transition of Cambridge College Puerto Rico Programs to Bay Path University. The Coordinator must provide excellent customer service to students, faculty, staff, and visitors in a professional, courteous, and responsive manner. This position requires on-campus presence on weekdays and weekends as operationally needed. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Dean & Administrative Support Serve as the primary point of contact in the Dean's office, managing inquiries, scheduling, correspondence, and daily office operations with professionalism and discretion. Manage the Dean's calendar and coordinate all campus and departmental meetings. Draft letters, reports, proposals, and communications; Support the Dean in project management, maintaining work plans, tracking deliverables, and preparing reports and research as needed. Provide translation support for communications, documents, and correspondence in both English and Spanish as needed by the Dean and campus operations. Handle confidential information with the highest level of discretion regarding sensitive matters. Support other staff and faculty as directed by the Dean Regulatory Support the Dean in liaising with Puerto Rican government agencies, coordinating meetings, preparing and submitting required documentation, and following up on pending authorizations. Gather and compile documentation from Bay Path University staff to support transition petitions under the name Cambridge College Puerto Rico at Bay Path University. Assist the Dean in reviewing academic program parity and preparing submissions to the Puerto Rico Board of Postsecondary Institutions (Junta de Instituciones Postsecundarias de Puerto Rico). Assist with translation of regulatory documents and communications with government agencies as needed. Student Support & Event Planning Provide responsive customer service to students, proactively resolving concerns and connecting them with appropriate University resources. Maintain campus academic calendars, enrollment records, and program data; generate reports as needed. Coordinate and deliver student orientations, including mandatory sessions related to the University integration and attestation process. Lead the planning and execution of Commencement, managing all logistics from start to finish, including preparation of graduation spreadsheets, graduate surveys, and data analysis to support ceremony planning. Coordinate campus and virtual events, including student award ceremonies and community partnership events. Attend trainings as required. Perform any other duties or tasks as assigned by the University. Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor's degree required; advanced degree or equivalent experience preferred. Minimum of three to five (3–5) years of progressively responsible administrative experience, preferably in higher education. Bilingual fluency in English and Spanish (written and verbal) required. Ability to work on weekends as required. Experience with Puerto Rican government agencies or postsecondary regulatory processes. preferred Background in student services, academic affairs, or enrollment management in higher education preferred. Strong organizational, communication, and project management skills; ability to work independently and handle sensitive matters with discretion. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and university administrative systems; familiarity with CANVAS or similar LMS a plus. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with all members of the University community including students, faculty, staff, and administrators Ability to adhere to University policies and procedures. Ability to handle confidential information with discretion and within FERPA and HIPAA guidelines. All new employees must complete the FERPA, Anti-Harassment, and any other required online trainings within 15 days of employment. General knowledge of the University’s mission, purpose and goals and the role this position plays in achieving those goals. Share job details to About BAY PATH UNIVERSITY Bay Path University is a private comprehensive university with a bold and innovative spirit. Known for its commitment to providing a practical and career-focused education, Bay Path offers a residential bachelors degree for women only on its Longmeadow, Massachusetts campus, as well as bachelors, masters and doctoral programs for both men and women on campuses in East Longmeadow, Boston, Guaynabo, Puerto Rico and online. In 2024, Bay Path expanded its reach and program offerings through the acquisition of Cambridge College, increasing its enrollment to approximately 5,000 learners, gaining new locations, strengthening its online presence, and broadening its career-focused programs. Respected for strong allied health, education and business programs, accessible online options, and a supportive community, Bay Path is an appealing choice for many students. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3A2948EF284B8722FEE42E01FB156C27/jobs/116179": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Advancement Services and Operations",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Advancement Services and Operations You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Director of Advancement Services and Operations Hybrid   •   Longmeadow, MA 01106 Apply Overview Salary Range $52,552.50 - $63,160.50 Salary/year Position Type Full-Time Salaried Apply Description Supervisor: Associate Director for Donor Relations Status: Full-time, 37.5 hours/week Hours: 8 : 30 am - 5:00 pm Job Location: Longmeadow Campus/Hybrid Exempt (Yes/No): Yes JOB SUMMARY: Reporting to the Associate Director for Donor Relations, the Assistant Director of Advancement Services and Operations will oversee daily gift processing and receipts; update and manage Advancement’s CRM (Blackbaud Raiser's Edge NXT), including data hygiene projects and improvements; provide regular financial/accounting reports and reconciliations; and support the development of donor fund and gift reports. In support of Institutional Advancement prospect management, the Assistant Director will assist with prospect screening, prospect reports, and moves management, updating prospect records to accurately reflect ratings and activities. The Assistant Director will provide crucial assistance and a strong foundation for the Advancement staff’s efforts to manage, identify, cultivate, solicit, and steward Major Gift prospects and Annual Giving donors. The Assistant Director will assist in the development and design of reports to support departmental needs. This detail-oriented position will produce a variety of reports on a regular basis and maintain an assortment of lists in support of Advancement needs and activities. The successful candidate will work with high-level, often confidential information and operate under strict standards and tight deadlines. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS: Serve as the administrator of Raiser's Edge, including but not limited to Raiser's Edge Online Express, Blackbaud NetCommunity (BBNC), ResearchPoint-Target Analytics, and the affiliated modules and tools associated with Blackbaud Raiser's Edge NXT. Perform giving trend analysis. Assist the Vice President of Advancement with reports for the Board of Trustees and Institutional Advancement Committee. Work with the Associate Director for Donor Relations on the creation of new fund records. Facilitate the creation of new pledges and administrative paperwork. Partner with key university functional areas, e.g. Finance, Student Financial Services, Academic Affairs, and Student Affairs. Responsible for accurate gift entry , batch preparation for the finance office, and gift receipt production and oversight. This position records gifts, grants, and pledges to the university, ensuring compliance with IRS tax laws and regulations, accounting best practices, and CASE standards. Independently produce , reconcile, organize and maintain reports from Raiser's Edge and various other lists, including, but not limited to, regular gift reports, alumni lists, mailing lists, prospect management reports, monthly gift reports for the finance office, monthly LYBUNT lists, annual pledge review and other reports and lists as requested by supervisor . In support of the prospect management system, provide donor/prospect screening/research and donor reports for Advancement staff as requested, for potential visits and events, alerting staff of any changes in constituent vital information, including gifts, news or activities . Design and revise reports to be pulled from Raiser’s Edge in support of department goals and activities. Supervise the revision and production of timely and appropriate receipts and other assigned letters. Accurately maintain Raiser’s Edge , ensuring consistency and following best practices. Maintain active knowledge of university gift acceptance policies and procedures. Manage and maintain Virtual Engagement Officers (VEO) portfolios by updating records, importing VEO actions into Raiser's Edge, and ensuring accurate and timely data entry based on information received from VEOs. Assist immediate supervisor in cross-training Advancement staff and support new Institutional Advancement employee orientation. Participate in department meetings, university committees and professional development programs as required. Attend training(s) as required. Perform any other duties or tasks as assigned by the university . SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES : Student-workers as relevant Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS : Minimum of associate’s degree required, bachelor's degree preferred. Experience in a fundraising environment or related advancement. experience, preferably for a nonprofit or higher education institution. Experience with gift processing and CRM desired (ex . Jenzabar, Salesforce, Raiser's Edge). Excellent Microsoft Office skills, including proficiency in Excel (knowledge of Pivot Tables a plus) and Word mail merge. Able to utilize the Internet (including social media) and provided resources to conduct constituent research. Proven excellent organizational skills. Demonstrated ability to prioritize workload, manage changing priorities, work with frequent interruptions and meet deadlines. Able to work both independently and collaboratively to manage multiple responsibilities. Initiative, problem solving skills and high attention to detail and accuracy. Good judgment, confidentiality and discretion in communicating with colleagues and constituents. Strong communication and customer service skills. Ability to adhere to university policies and procedures. Excellent interpersonal, written and oral communication skills. Ability to work independently and within a team. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with all members of the university community including students, faculty, staff, and administrators. Ability to handle confidential information with discretion and within FERPA and HIPAA guidelines. Completion of the FERPA, Anti-Harassment, and any other required online trainings within 15 days of employment. General knowledge of the university's mission, purpose and goals and the role this position plays in achieving those goals . Share job details to About BAY PATH UNIVERSITY Bay Path University is a private comprehensive university with a bold and innovative spirit. Known for its commitment to providing a practical and career-focused education, Bay Path offers a residential bachelors degree for women only on its Longmeadow, Massachusetts campus, as well as bachelors, masters and doctoral programs for both men and women on campuses in East Longmeadow, Boston, Guaynabo, Puerto Rico and online. In 2024, Bay Path expanded its reach and program offerings through the acquisition of Cambridge College, increasing its enrollment to approximately 5,000 learners, gaining new locations, strengthening its online presence, and broadening its career-focused programs. Respected for strong allied health, education and business programs, accessible online options, and a supportive community, Bay Path is an appealing choice for many students. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3A2948EF284B8722FEE42E01FB156C27/jobs/115641": {
      "title": "Professional Advisor",
      "description": "Professional Advisor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Professional Advisor Longmeadow, MA 01106 Apply Overview Salary Range $38,000.00 - $46,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full-Time Hourly Apply Description Supervisor: Director of Advising (Trad) Position Code: PFADV Status: FT Hours : M-F 8:30am - 5:00 pm, including weekends and evenings as necessary Job Location: Longmeadow, Hybrid Exempt (Yes/No): No JOB SUMMARY: The Professional Advisor works in a culture of collaboration with a faculty, career and peer advisor in a shared advising model, serving as Team Lead.  The Professional Advisor is dedicated to student success, serving as a trusted and consistent resource to students, providing accurate and reliable information to assist them in meeting academic and personal goals. The Professional Advisor possesses a high attention to detail, demonstrates strong interpersonal skills, embraces advising technology, thinks critically and possesses an understanding of college student development theory. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Provide developmental advising for a caseload of 200-300 students from enrollment to graduation. Work collaboratively with a comprehensive advising team including faculty, career, and peer advisors. Engage in purposeful discussion with students to learn about course performance and interests, providing accurate and current curricular information to undergraduate students, assisting in the development of achievable academic goals and degree plans. Assist students with major exploration, sharing curricular and co-curricular opportunities. Assist students in clarifying their understanding of academic skills, strengths and challenges, personal values, abilities, and goals. Communicate important University policies and procedures to students. Coordinate and implement outreach interventions for at risk students focused on student success and retention. Monitor and advise students to ensure satisfactory progress, including warnings, probations and holds; following up accordingly. Create a welcoming environment that is inclusive of all students from all backgrounds. Utilize technology to identify and support at risk students, using data analytics. Maintain complete and accurate documentation of all student interactions, designing completion plans. Assist students in learning University planning tools such as the student portal, learning management system, and degree auditing and course registration systems. Stay abreast of changing institutional information including new programs, course changes and important dates. Make referrals for students to appropriate campus resources. Present at prospective student events. Understand FERPA policies and regulations. Participate in relevant training and professional development opportunities. Submit mid-term and end of year reports to the Director of Advising. Serve on relevant universities committees. Attend trainings as required. Perform any other duties or tasks as assigned by the University. Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS: Master’s degree in student affairs, counseling or related field. Understanding of student development theory and developmental advising and experience counseling students in curricular exploration preferred. Experience working with diverse student populations in a higher education setting. Should possess excellent interpersonal, written and oral communication skills, attention to detail with the ability to establish and maintain effective relationships with students, faculty and staff. Ability to work independently and within a team. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with all members of the University community including students, faculty, staff, and administrators Ability to adhere to University policies and procedures. Ability to handle confidential information with discretion and within FERPA and HIPAA guidelines. All new employees must complete the FERPA, Anti-Harassment, and any other required online trainings within 15 days of employment. General knowledge of the University’s mission, purpose and goals and the role this position plays in achieving those goals. Share job details to About BAY PATH UNIVERSITY Bay Path University is a private comprehensive university with a bold and innovative spirit. Known for its commitment to providing a practical and career-focused education, Bay Path offers a residential bachelors degree for women only on its Longmeadow, Massachusetts campus, as well as bachelors, masters and doctoral programs for both men and women on campuses in East Longmeadow, Boston, Guaynabo, Puerto Rico and online. In 2024, Bay Path expanded its reach and program offerings through the acquisition of Cambridge College, increasing its enrollment to approximately 5,000 learners, gaining new locations, strengthening its online presence, and broadening its career-focused programs. Respected for strong allied health, education and business programs, accessible online options, and a supportive community, Bay Path is an appealing choice for many students. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3A2948EF284B8722FEE42E01FB156C27/jobs/115634": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Graduate Admissions",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Graduate Admissions You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Director of Graduate Admissions Hybrid   •   Longmeadow, MA 01106 Apply Overview Salary Range $44,908.50 - $53,976.00 Salary/year Position Type Full-Time Salaried Job Shift Day Apply Description JOB SUMMARY: Reporting to the Director of Graduate Admissions, the Assistant Director (AD) is responsible for the recruitment and enrollment of qualified graduate students for all assigned programs. This role represents Bay Path University to prospective students and organizations and works to increase inquiries and convert applications into enrolled students. A successful AD exhibits superior customer service skills and professionalism throughout daily interactions and communications with students including phone calls, emails, information sessions, and other events, both virtual and in person. This position also creates and implements recruitment strategies to reach prospective students through events, referrals, online and print communications, and outreaches to businesses and organizations. The Assistant Director must demonstrate an ability to work independently as well as collaboratively with team members, faculty, students, alumni, administrators and staff. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS: ● Ability to work in a fast-paced environment and meet qualified enrollment goals. ● Manage prospective students through the enrollment pipeline from inquiry through registration; advise on application process and policies. Uphold a high level of customer service to maintain satisfaction. ● Initiate, cultivate and manage the development of external contacts and databases including the development of relationships with professional organizations to promote graduate programs. ● Strong conversion skills through all stages of the enrollment funnel to meet or exceed enrollment goals. ● Represent Bay Path University at college fairs, professional organizations, and conferences to network with potential students. ● Utilize the Salesforce system in effectively tracking all outreaches to inquiries and applicants. ● Assist with the implementation of recruitment and promotional events for the Graduate School. These promotional events may include, but are not limited Page 1 of 5 Assistant Director of Graduate Admissions Revised: February 4, 2021 to, arranging speaking engagements for faculty, presentations at local business/professional organizations, and information sessions on campus and virtual events. ● Actively engage potential students in conversations via phone, in person meetings, virtual meetings and Agendize appointments. ● Instruct prospective applicants on admissions requirements for specific programs and inform of any program prerequisites. Complete application review and regulate flow of applications to program directors or faculty designated as interviewers. ● Handle a wide variety of tasks in a busy service-oriented atmosphere; establish priorities utilizing excellent organizational ability. ● Conduct group presentations for prospective students, business professionals, advisors and other contacts about specific programs. OTHER RESPONSIBILITIES: ● Attend trainings as required. ● Perform any other duties or tasks as assigned by the University. ● If you operate a University owned, leased or personal vehicle at any time while performing your duties you must follow all policies and procedures outlined in the Operations Manual. You must have a valid driver’s license and must successfully pass the online safe Driving Course and driving record check at time of hire and annually thereafter. Additionally, you must report any driving offense, on or off company time, which causes a loss, suspension, or any other change in your license status. You must report this change within one business day of the offense. You can report this change to the Human Resource Department or your direct supervisor. Failure to do so can lead to disciplinary action, up to and including terminations. This list of essential job functions and other responsibilities is representative of those duties and responsibilities that are required of this position. However, the list is not to be considered as all-inclusive. A supervisor or director may assign other duties and/or other duties at alternate locations to meet mission requirements of the University and cooperation of all personnel is expected to carry out the mission. SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES: ● N/A  PHYSICAL DEMANDS AND WORK ENVIRONMENT: The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. ● Ability to stand, walk and/or sit and continuously perform essential job functions. ● Ability to grasp, lift and/or carry or otherwise move lightweight objects. ● Ability to walk up and down stairs and walking significant distances between and within University buildings. ● Perform tasks requiring bending, stooping, and kneeling. ● Sufficient manual dexterity in both hands to operate variety of office related equipment including; computer, telephone, copier, fax, calculator, and the like. ● Visual ability corrected, to assure accuracy of all documents produced or disseminated from this position. ● Audio ability corrected, to hear telephone, fax and any emergency related alarms such as fire alarm. This position requires standing, sitting and walking; minimal pulling, pushing, lifting, stretching, kneeling, and lifting up to 20 lbs. Qualifications ● Bachelor’s degree required in a related field; Master’s degree preferred. ● Excellent oral and written communication skills needed. ● Experience working in a sales or marketing related position or in the recruitment of students in a college setting. Previous Career Development, Human Resources, Sales, Admissions or Enrollment Management preferred. ● Experience working with or advising students at the undergraduate or graduate level helpful. ● Ability and willingness to travel and work evenings and weekends as needed. ● Strong analytical abilities, maturity, and a high energy level. ● Demonstrated experience with Microsoft Office programs required. ● Sensitivity to the concerns of diverse student populations. ● Valid U.S. driver's license is required. ● Must successfully pass the online safe Driving Course (within 15 days of hire) and driving record check at time of hire and annually thereafter. ● Demonstrated ability to perform detailed project work with an emphasis on teamwork, working with students, faculty, staff and clients in a professional manner. ● Ability to work under pressure. ● Ability to understand the impact of student enrollment on the success of the institution. ● Ability to adhere to University policies and procedures. ● Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with all members of the University community including students, faculty, staff, and administrators ● Ability to adhere to University policies and procedures. ● Ability to handle confidential information with discretion and within FERPA and HIPAA guidelines. ● All new employees must complete the FERPA, Anti-Harassment, and any other required online trainings within 15 days of employment. ● General knowledge of the University’s mission, purpose and goals and the role this position plays in achieving those goals. Share job details to About BAY PATH UNIVERSITY Bay Path University is a private comprehensive university with a bold and innovative spirit. Known for its commitment to providing a practical and career-focused education, Bay Path offers a residential bachelors degree for women only on its Longmeadow, Massachusetts campus, as well as bachelors, masters and doctoral programs for both men and women on campuses in East Longmeadow, Boston, Guaynabo, Puerto Rico and online. In 2024, Bay Path expanded its reach and program offerings through the acquisition of Cambridge College, increasing its enrollment to approximately 5,000 learners, gaining new locations, strengthening its online presence, and broadening its career-focused programs. Respected for strong allied health, education and business programs, accessible online options, and a supportive community, Bay Path is an appealing choice for many students. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3A2948EF284B8722FEE42E01FB156C27/jobs/115519": {
      "title": "Online Adjunct Faculty - Special Education (SPE 530)",
      "description": "Online Adjunct Faculty - Special Education (SPE 530) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Online Adjunct Faculty - Special Education (SPE 530) Apply Overview Salary Range $500.00 - $1,200.00 Salary Position Type Adjunct Faculty Apply Description Graduate Online Synchronous Course in Special Education Course Title : Curriculum Design and Assessment Course Description: Using a case study approach, students learn to select, construct, use and interpret non-discriminatory and developmentally appropriate assessments relevant to diverse learners with mild and moderate disabilities. The Massachusetts Frameworks are used to guide decisions in both curriculum and instruction and ways to prepare and maintain students in general education. Course assignments are designed to help students gain an understanding of educational terminology utilized with students with special needs; and differentiated instruction and ways to implement meaningful instruction for all students, especially students with disabilities by designing and modifying curriculum and instructional materials. Compensation: $500 - $1,200 per credit. Adjunct faculty rates vary, depending on academic discipline and the course's credit load and level. Qualifications Special Education Course Instructors must meet the following criteria: Hold a current Massachusetts Educator Professional License in Moderate Disabilities, Severe Disabilities, or a closely related field. A minimum of a Master's Degree in Special Education or a closely related field Minimum of 5 years teaching in special education within a K12 public school setting A minimum of 3 years administering, scoring, and interpreting assessments within special education. Available to hold weekly virtual Zoom class meetings. Ability to adhere to University policies and procedures. Ability to handle confidential information with discretion and within FERPA and HIPAA guidelines. All new employees must complete the FERPA, Anti-Harassment, and any other required online trainings within 15 days of employment. General knowledge of the University’s mission, purpose, and goals and the role this position plays in achieving those goals. Share job details to About BAY PATH UNIVERSITY Bay Path University is a private comprehensive university with a bold and innovative spirit. Known for its commitment to providing a practical and career-focused education, Bay Path offers a residential bachelors degree for women only on its Longmeadow, Massachusetts campus, as well as bachelors, masters and doctoral programs for both men and women on campuses in East Longmeadow, Boston, Guaynabo, Puerto Rico and online. In 2024, Bay Path expanded its reach and program offerings through the acquisition of Cambridge College, increasing its enrollment to approximately 5,000 learners, gaining new locations, strengthening its online presence, and broadening its career-focused programs. Respected for strong allied health, education and business programs, accessible online options, and a supportive community, Bay Path is an appealing choice for many students. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
