    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3A2948EF284B8722FEE42E01FB156C27/jobs/115512": {
      "title": "Online Adjunct Faculty - Special Education (SPE 548)",
      "description": "Online Adjunct Faculty - Special Education (SPE 548) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Online Adjunct Faculty - Special Education (SPE 548) Fully Remote   •   East Longmeadow, MA 01028 Apply Overview Salary Range $500.00 - $1,200.00 Salary Position Type Adjunct Faculty Apply Description Graduate Level Synchronous Online SEI Course Course Title: Reading and Language Arts for English Language Learners Course Description: This course is designed to introduce the developing teacher to reading instruction and the development of a reading/writing community in English for English Learners (ELs).  This course is designed to promote continuous improvement in educator practice, and to build confidence and familiarity with research-proven practices for working with ELLs.  This course is framed around two module areas: A) English Language Learners, Language Acquisition, and Sheltered English Instruction, and B) Academic Language and Literacy Development in the SEI Classroom. Compensation: $500 - $1,200 per credit. Adjunct faculty pay rates vary, depending on the academic discipline and the course's credit load and level. Qualifications SEI Course Instructor must: Hold a current Massachusetts Educator Professional License with SEI Endorsement, preferably a Massachusetts ESL Educator License A minimum of a Master's Degree in English as a Second Language or a closely related field Minimum of 5 years teaching multilingual learners in a K12 public school setting A minimum of 2 years teaching an SEI (Sheltered English Immersion) course Available to hold weekly virtual Zoom class meetings on Saturdays from 8:30 AM to 11:30 AM Ability to adhere to University policies and procedures. Ability to handle confidential information with discretion and within FERPA and HIPAA guidelines. All new employees must complete the FERPA, Anti-Harassment, and any other required online trainings within 15 days of employment. General knowledge of the University’s mission, purpose, and goals and the role this position plays in achieving those goals. Share job details to About BAY PATH UNIVERSITY Bay Path University is a private comprehensive university with a bold and innovative spirit. Known for its commitment to providing a practical and career-focused education, Bay Path offers a residential bachelors degree for women only on its Longmeadow, Massachusetts campus, as well as bachelors, masters and doctoral programs for both men and women on campuses in East Longmeadow, Boston, Guaynabo, Puerto Rico and online. In 2024, Bay Path expanded its reach and program offerings through the acquisition of Cambridge College, increasing its enrollment to approximately 5,000 learners, gaining new locations, strengthening its online presence, and broadening its career-focused programs. Respected for strong allied health, education and business programs, accessible online options, and a supportive community, Bay Path is an appealing choice for many students. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
