    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3A2948EF284B8722FEE42E01FB156C27/jobs/110265": {
      "title": "Assistant Director Advising Operations and Outreach",
      "description": "Assistant Director Advising Operations and Outreach You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Assistant Director Advising Operations and Outreach Hybrid   •   Longmeadow, MA 01106 Apply Overview Salary Range $52,000.00 - $63,000.00 Salary Position Type Full-Time Salaried Job Shift Day Apply Description Supervisor: Dean for Retention and Advising Position Code: ADAOO Status: FT Hours : M-F 8:30 am - 5:00 pm Job Location: Longmeadow, Hybrid Exempt (Yes/No): Yes JOB SUMMARY: The Assistant Director of Advising Operations and Outreach is responsible for the University’s student success and advising management systems across student populations. This includes supporting software applications used to support student advising and retention.  Working with a team of professional advisors, the Assistant Director ensures the University systems meet the needs of the student success and retention efforts, streamlining communication and support to students and advisors.  The Assistant Director will leverage data and technology to coordinate meaningful outreach to students throughout their educational journey. The Assistant Director will assist in the development and review of advising related assessment, developing regular reports related to student success and persistence. The Assistant Director will also provide advising to a caseload of up to 100 students. Working collaboratively with student financial services, Dean of Students, information technology, admissions and advising colleagues, the Assistant Director develops and oversees advising operations calendars and communication plans, ensuring processes and proactive outreach occur in a timely manner.  The Assistant Director works collaboratively with  the Director for Advising and Student Success and the Director of BPO Advising and in developing and implementing semester engagement activities such as welcome events, annual family picnic, advising drop in hours, online communities for student parents and caregivers, commencement and celebratory events to name a few. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Maintain an assigned caseload of students, providing holistic advising, proactive outreach, course registration support, and referrals to campus resources as appropriate. Assist Dean, leading all administrative operations for non BPO Advising and Retention efforts, including student hires, budget management, departmental communications and calendaring, website, social media, retention tracking and reporting, and system optimization efforts. Develop business practices, policies, and procedures for students, faculty and staff on the use of student success management and advising tools. Coordinate communications related to business practices, policies and procedures of student success management and advising tools. Apply project management processes to ensure successful project implementation and execution of advising and  student success operation ensuring program deliverables are met and activities are completed in a timely manner. Create and maintain faculty and staff user accounts. Create and execute semester and yearlong communication and event plans for the Advising Center. Coordinate work through cross-functional teams, including student affairs staff involved in case management, IT, Academic Deans, faculty and Career Advisors to improve integration with disparate systems and data courses. Review and evaluate program effectiveness; assist in data management and compilation of reports. Work with vendors to research issues and test functionality of the systems, and implement ongoing systems improvements and enhancements. Coordinate development and implementation of necessary trainings related to student success management tools. Coordinate advising operations and processes including staff onboarding, training and operational materials, new student onboarding, registration, early alert reporting, midterm grade review (Trad), add/drop, university withdrawals, non-par processes, and post session outreach, and assessment. Pull, analyze, and distribute reports using Salesforce, Jenzabar, Google Suite, and PowerBI to inform decision-making and track progress toward retention goals. Contribute to the planning and implementation of student success initiatives, ensuring they are data-informed and measurable. Assist in developing or administering virtual and in person events such as orientation and BPO 099, webinars, ceremonies, graduation activities. Assist Dean in leveraging AI and predictive analytics to identify at-risk students, developing communications plans for proactive outreach. Maintain thorough and accurate documentation of activity utilizing technological tools such as a CRM and Student Information System. Assist in the development of data dashboards and tracking to inform advising and retention efforts. Evaluate processes and procedures and make recommendations for continuous improvement in the student experience by thoughtfully utilizing technology, customization and workflow design. Support recruitment, marketing, admissions, orientation and retention activities as needed. Select, Train and Supervise a Team of Peer Mentors to provide support and outreach to new Longmeadow students.  Work collaboratively with the Director for Advising and Student Success in developing engagement activities.  Assess all peer mentor related programs. Prepare a mid year and end of year report. Others duties as assigned. Attend trainings as required. Perform any other duties or tasks as assigned by the University. KNOWLEDGE AND SKILLS: Effectively prioritizing work requests, multi-tasking and time management. Providing technical assistance to others and communicating technical concepts and ideas to diverse populations both verbally and in writing. Ability to engage in systems thinking, configure systems for consistency with institutional policies and procedures. Ability to work in a fast paced environment, meeting deadlines. Ability to manipulate and analyze data; staying abreast of technology changes related to student success. Establish and maintain cooperation, understanding, trust and credibility Possess excellent customer service skills. Read, understand, and follow application specific documentation of procedures and instructions. Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor’s degree required and 5-7 years’ experience. Experience with project management software required; experience with Jenzabar and Salesforce preferred. Experience in troubleshooting and analysis principles, application design principles and scheduling systems. Strong interpersonal, written and oral communication skills. Experience working in a higher education setting is preferred. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with all members of the University community including students, faculty, staff, and administrators. Ability to adhere to University policies and procedures. Ability to handle confidential information with discretion and within FERPA and HIPAA guidelines. All new employees must complete the FERPA, Anti-Harassment, and any other required online trainings within 15 days of employment. General knowledge of the University’s mission, purpose and goals and the role this position plays in achieving those goals. Share job details to About BAY PATH UNIVERSITY Bay Path University is a private comprehensive university with a bold and innovative spirit. Known for its commitment to providing a practical and career-focused education, Bay Path offers a residential bachelors degree for women only on its Longmeadow, Massachusetts campus, as well as bachelors, masters and doctoral programs for both men and women on campuses in East Longmeadow, Boston, Guaynabo, Puerto Rico and online. In 2024, Bay Path expanded its reach and program offerings through the acquisition of Cambridge College, increasing its enrollment to approximately 5,000 learners, gaining new locations, strengthening its online presence, and broadening its career-focused programs. Respected for strong allied health, education and business programs, accessible online options, and a supportive community, Bay Path is an appealing choice for many students. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3A2948EF284B8722FEE42E01FB156C27/jobs/108398": {
      "title": "Director of Enrollment Marketing (CC)",
      "description": "Director of Enrollment Marketing (CC) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Director of Enrollment Marketing (CC) Longmeadow, MA 01106 Apply Overview Salary Range $60,000.00 - $75,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full-Time Salaried Apply Description Supervisor: Sr. Director of Enrollment Marketing Status: Full Time Job Location: Hybrid Longmeadow or Remote if beyond 45 miles Exempt (Yes/No): Yes JOB SUMMARY : The Director of Enrollment Marketing provides strategic leadership for enrollment marketing initiatives for their assigned divisions / programs to meet enrollment goals. Reporting to the Sr. Director of Enrollment Marketing, this position develops and executes integrated marketing strategies with a strong emphasis on digital marketing, email marketing, lead generation, and marketing automation. The Director collaborates closely with Enrollment Management, and Academic Affairs, and external agency partners to develop campaigns that attract, engage, and convert prospective students throughout the enrollment funnel. This role is responsible for optimizing marketing performance through data analysis, audience segmentation, CRM strategy, and continuous improvement. Essential Responsibilities Develop and execute integrated enrollment marketing strategies that support recruitment and enrollment goals for assigned divisions and programs. Lead multi-channel marketing campaigns across digital, email, web, social media, paid media, search, display, and other channels to generate inquiries, applications, and enrollments. Develop and oversee enrollment communication strategies that engage prospective students throughout the enrollment lifecycle—from inquiry through enrollment—including targeted email marketing campaigns, automated communication flows, and personalized messaging that improves engagement, conversion, and enrollment yield. Partner with the Enrollment Marketing Systems team to optimize CRM workflows, audience segmentation, lead management, marketing automation, campaign tracking, and reporting to support effective recruitment and personalized student communications. Monitor and optimize digital marketing performance, website conversion, email engagement, and enrollment funnel metrics through data analysis, A/B testing, and continuous improvement to maximize marketing effectiveness and return on investment. Collaborate with Enrollment Management, Academic Affairs, Communications, and external agency partners to develop integrated recruitment campaigns that align with institutional priorities, enrollment goals, and brand standards. Partner with web and creative teams to develop and optimize enrollment-focused content, landing pages, digital experiences, and calls to action that strengthen prospective student engagement and conversion. Manage assigned marketing budgets, agency relationships, project timelines, and campaign execution, ensuring initiatives are completed on time, within budget, and aligned with strategic priorities. Drive innovation by evaluating emerging enrollment marketing trends, digital technologies, and artificial intelligence (AI) tools to enhance recruitment strategies, personalize the prospective student experience, improve operational efficiency, and strengthen marketing performance while ensuring technology complements, not replaces, the human-centered student experience. Prepare and present campaign performance reports, key performance indicators, market insights, and strategic recommendations to senior leadership, using data to inform decision-making and continuous improvement. Qualifications Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Marketing, Communications, Business, or a related field required; Master's degree preferred. Minimum of five (5) years of progressively responsible experience in marketing, enrollment marketing, or higher education marketing. Demonstrated success developing and executing integrated, multi-channel marketing campaigns with a strong emphasis on digital marketing, lead generation, and enrollment growth. Experience developing and managing email marketing strategies, lifecycle communications, and automated communication flows that guide prospective students through the enrollment funnel. Experience with CRM systems and marketing automation platforms; Salesforce and Marketing Cloud Account Engagement (Pardot) experience strongly preferred. Strong knowledge of digital marketing, including Google Analytics, Google Ads, Meta advertising, SEO/SEM, website optimization, and campaign performance analysis. Demonstrated analytical skills with the ability to interpret marketing data, measure campaign performance, identify trends, and make data-driven recommendations to improve results. Experience writing, editing, and developing compelling marketing content for websites, email campaigns, digital advertising, and other enrollment communications. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite, Adobe Creative Cloud, Canva, and other marketing technologies. Experience managing multiple priorities, projects, and deadlines in a fast-paced, collaborative environment. Experience working effectively with external marketing agencies and vendor partners to develop and execute successful campaigns. Excellent written, verbal, interpersonal, and active listening skills, with the ability to build strong relationships across the institution. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively with Enrollment Management, Academic Affairs, Communications, and other cross-functional stakeholders to achieve shared enrollment goals. Strong organizational, project management, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work independently while managing competing priorities. Demonstrated ability to effectively communicate and advance an institution's mission and value proposition through integrated marketing and digital communication strategies. Innovative, entrepreneurial, and results-oriented, with the ability to evaluate and responsibly leverage emerging technologies, including artificial intelligence (AI), to enhance recruitment strategies, personalize prospective student communications, improve operational efficiency, and strengthen the student experience without replacing meaningful human engagement. Ability to adhere to University policies and procedures. Ability to handle confidential information with discretion and within FERPA and HIPAA guidelines. All new employees must complete the FERPA, Anti-Harassment, and any other required online trainings within 15 days of employment. Should have demonstrated ability to build working relationships with people having a wide variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences different from ones’ own. General knowledge of the University’s mission, purpose and goals and the role this position plays in achieving those goals. Share job details to About BAY PATH UNIVERSITY Bay Path University is a private comprehensive university with a bold and innovative spirit. Known for its commitment to providing a practical and career-focused education, Bay Path offers a residential bachelors degree for women only on its Longmeadow, Massachusetts campus, as well as bachelors, masters and doctoral programs for both men and women on campuses in East Longmeadow, Boston, Guaynabo, Puerto Rico and online. In 2024, Bay Path expanded its reach and program offerings through the acquisition of Cambridge College, increasing its enrollment to approximately 5,000 learners, gaining new locations, strengthening its online presence, and broadening its career-focused programs. Respected for strong allied health, education and business programs, accessible online options, and a supportive community, Bay Path is an appealing choice for many students. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3A2948EF284B8722FEE42E01FB156C27/jobs/100143": {
      "title": "Principal Faculty - Clinical",
      "description": "Principal Faculty - Clinical You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Principal Faculty - Clinical East Longmeadow, MA 01028 Apply Overview Salary Range $95,000.00 - $100,000.00 Salary Position Type Full-Time Faculty Apply Description JOB TITLE : Principal Faculty - Clinical Supervisor: Program Director Status: Full-Time, 12 months Job Location: East Longmeadow Exempt (Yes/No): Yes JOB SUMMARY: The Principal Faculty – Clinical, serves in the clinical education portion of the PA program in collaboration with the Director of Clinical Education. The position contributes to the development, scheduling, and evaluation of supervised clinical practice experience (SCPE) sites, ensuring alignment with accreditation standards, program outcomes and competencies. Maintains clinical site relationships, oversees student progress, addresses concerns, coordinates schedules and compliance, conducts site visits, and supports students and preceptors during the clinical phase. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Coordinates and oversees clinical clerkships, including scheduling, site acquisition, and preceptor recruitment. Maintains relationships and contracts with clinical affiliates, monitors site quality, and ensures accreditation compliance. Manages clinical curriculum evaluation, databases, and student performance tracking, providing remediation as needed. Organizes student orientations, return-to-campus activities, and site visits, collaborating with faculty and leadership to support student success and program outcomes. Didactic Contribute to curriculum design, instructional materials, and learning objectives. Support program evaluation, recordkeeping, and data analysis for accreditation or reporting. Teach assigned didactic courses, assess student performance, and provide remediation when needed. Actively participate in lab sessions, practical examinations, skills courses and small groups. Faculty Participate in the development, review, and revision, as needed, of the program’s mission statement, goals, and competencies. Participate in the ongoing ARC-PA self-assessment process, accreditation activities or actions, meetings, and on-site evaluation. Engage in teaching, scholarship, and service activities as defined in the Faculty Manual. Full-time faculty members not serving as chairs of departments, directors of programs, assistant or associate deans usually shall be required to teach 24 credit hours or their equivalent per academic year. Develop proficiency in programmatic systems, such as but limited to: CANVAS, CASPA, Exxact, PAEA and Exam Soft, or equivalent programmatic systems. Serve as an ambassador for the PA Program through participation in service activities of the University and PA Program. Participate in the identification, recruitment, and selection of qualified applicants. Identify sources for and participate in the preparation and implementation of grants and contracts supportive of the activities of the University and PA Program. Serve on University and PA Program faculty committees as/when appointed or elected. Attend and participate in required university activities such as, but not limited to, university graduation, faculty development sessions, assessment day and faculty committee work. Attend and participate in Departmental meetings and annual retreats. Attend and participate in program activities such as, but not limited to, Information Sessions, Admissions activities, White Coat Ceremony, PA Graduation, and external committee obligations. Participate in the search process activities of the University and PA Program. Participate in NEASC accreditation activities as assigned. Participate in local, state, and national professional organizations for own professional development and to ensure program excellence and appropriateness of curriculum and instruction, and its application to clinical instruction. Perform other duties assigned by the University and Program. Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS: Current NCCPA certification. Current state licensure. A minimum of three years clinical experience. Master’s Degree required. Higher Education experience preferred. Strong organizational skills, ability to multitask, attention to detail, able to manage deadlines efficiently and effectively. Strong computer skills. Strong interpersonal and communication skills. The ability to responsibly handle sensitive and confidential information with discretion is critical. Valid driver’s license. Must successfully pass the online Defensive Driving Course and driving record check at time of hire and annually thereafter. General knowledge of the University’s mission, purpose and goals and the role of Principal Faculty- Clinical – Physician Assistant Program in achieving those goals. Share job details to About BAY PATH UNIVERSITY Bay Path University is a private comprehensive university with a bold and innovative spirit. Known for its commitment to providing a practical and career-focused education, Bay Path offers a residential bachelors degree for women only on its Longmeadow, Massachusetts campus, as well as bachelors, masters and doctoral programs for both men and women on campuses in East Longmeadow, Boston, Guaynabo, Puerto Rico and online. In 2024, Bay Path expanded its reach and program offerings through the acquisition of Cambridge College, increasing its enrollment to approximately 5,000 learners, gaining new locations, strengthening its online presence, and broadening its career-focused programs. Respected for strong allied health, education and business programs, accessible online options, and a supportive community, Bay Path is an appealing choice for many students. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3A2948EF284B8722FEE42E01FB156C27/jobs/85370": {
      "title": "Online Adjunct Faculty - Language Acquisitions and Literacy Development Part II (ESL 534)",
      "description": "Online Adjunct Faculty - Language Acquisitions and Literacy Development Part II (ESL 534) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Online Adjunct Faculty - Language Acquisitions and Literacy Development Part II (ESL 534) Apply Overview Salary Range $500.00 - $1,500.00 Salary Position Type Adjunct Faculty Apply Description ESL 534: Language Acquisitions and Literacy Development Part II This course will explore the development of listening, speaking, reading, and writing vocabulary, approaches and practices for developing writing skills, the writing process and formal elements of writing, oral/aural fluency in English at various proficiency levels, social and academic English and academic language for content areas, and the development of metalinguistic skills appropriate to cognitive, academic, and language proficiency levels. 12 hours of fieldwork experience required. Compensation: $500 - $1,200 per credit. Adjunct faculty pay rates vary, depending on the academic discipline and the course's credit load and level. Qualifications ESL Adjunct Instructors Hold a current Massachusetts Educator Professional License in one or more of the following fields: English as a Second Language, PreK-6, or English as a Second Language, 5-12, ELL Director. A minimum of a Master's Degree in ESL or a closely related field. A minimum of 5 years of K12 ESL education teaching or administration. Experience teaching online courses at the higher education level is preferred but not required. Ability to adhere to University policies and procedures. Ability to handle confidential information with discretion and within FERPA and HIPAA guidelines. All new employees must complete the FERPA, Anti-Harassment, and any other required online trainings within 15 days of employment. General knowledge of the University’s mission, purpose, and goals, and the role this position plays in achieving those goals. Share job details to About BAY PATH UNIVERSITY Bay Path University is a private comprehensive university with a bold and innovative spirit. Known for its commitment to providing a practical and career-focused education, Bay Path offers a residential bachelors degree for women only on its Longmeadow, Massachusetts campus, as well as bachelors, masters and doctoral programs for both men and women on campuses in East Longmeadow, Boston, Guaynabo, Puerto Rico and online. In 2024, Bay Path expanded its reach and program offerings through the acquisition of Cambridge College, increasing its enrollment to approximately 5,000 learners, gaining new locations, strengthening its online presence, and broadening its career-focused programs. Respected for strong allied health, education and business programs, accessible online options, and a supportive community, Bay Path is an appealing choice for many students. Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
